 "notes": "Spine: need -> PC-stopband hypothesis -> FRET photochromic film + film-on-PC architecture with stopband sweep -> PC assembly and spin-coating -> fcc colloidal crystal -> stopband position -> stopband/emission overlap gives ~40x enhancement -> differential ON vs OFF enhancement -> 7x contrast -> cycling and patterning -> conclusion. Two branches meet at a18: molecular switching (a11-a13) and photonic enhancement (a9-a17). Lost: Fig. S1b stopband red-shift after coating (supplement, not in packet); F1 schematic not opened. Key multimodal reading is spectral overlap on a shared wavelength axis (F2a, F5d), carried by proposed mm_op assess_feature_overlap. F5d only weakly supports the blue-shift explanation (a33 partial), so the mechanism for the differential enhancement (a17) is the weakest spine link. Stopband value for the 196 nm sample differs from the text (a24 contradicts); this does not change the optimum."
}